SUMMARY:New Mexico: PTE due
DESCRIPTION:New Mexico's pass-through entity return due date matches the fe
 deral due date for the entity type (March 15 for a calendar-year partnershi
 p/S-corp). New Mexico's "PTE" return is itself the state's elective entity-
 level tax return. Correction (this rebuild session): the cited source state
 s the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without addressing the 2026-
 specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday. Consistent with
  every other state in this data set that explicitly confirms a weekend-shif
 t policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delaware\, Montana\, Or
 egon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with the near-universal
  US government-deadline convention of shifting to the next business day\, t
 his entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted March 15\, 2026 to Ma
 rch 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the general shift conventi
 on\, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmation that this speci
 fic state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency. | New Mexico's 
 pass-through entity return due date matches the federal due date for the en
 tity type (March 15 for a calendar-year partnership/S-corp). New Mexico's "
 PTE" return is itself the state's elective entity-level tax return. Follows
  the federal extended due date - no separate New Mexico extension form requ
 ired for the base filing deadline. Correction (this rebuild session): the c
 ited source states the general rule (15th day of the 3rd month) without add
 ressing the 2026-specific weekend interaction - March 15\, 2026 is a Sunday
 . Consistent with every other state in this data set that explicitly confir
 ms a weekend-shift policy (e.g. Massachusetts\, New York\, Vermont\, Delawa
 re\, Montana\, Oregon all confirm shifting to March 16\, 2026)\, and with t
 he near-universal US government-deadline convention of shifting to the next
  business day\, this entry's date_2026 was corrected from an unshifted Marc
 h 15\, 2026 to March 16\, 2026. This is a computed application of the gener
 al shift convention\, not an independently re-fetched per-state confirmatio
 n that this specific state's statute shifts - flagged here for transparency
 . | Authority: New Mexico Taxation and Revenue Department\, direct fetch th
 is session: "on or before the due date of your federal return for the tax y
 ear." | Source: https://www.tax.newmexico.gov/businesses/corporate-income-f
 ranchise-tax-overview/pass-through-entity/ | This date is computed from a r
 ecurrence rule and may not reflect a later-announced change\; confirm again
 st the cited source before relying on it.
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
