SUMMARY:New Mexico: State sales & use tax return due
DESCRIPTION:Gross Receipts Tax (functions as sales tax) due 25th of month f
 ollowing the reporting period\; also semiannual (July 25 / January 25). | Q
 1 2026 (Jan-Mar) sales tax return\, applying New Mexico's quarterly-filer d
 ue-date rule: Gross Receipts Tax (functions as sales tax) due 25th of month
  following the reporting period\; also semiannual (July 25 / January 25). T
 his is a representative recurring pattern\, not a single annual deadline - 
 actual filing frequency (monthly/quarterly/annual) is assigned per business
  by the state. | Authority: Direct fetch of New Mexico's own tax agency sit
 e this session | Source: https://realfile.tax.newmexico.gov/trd-41413ins.pd
